Rule 1 (input tensor must have at least 2 dimensions to be a matrix or stack of matrices)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 3 (every dimension of the input tensor must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor must have at least 2 dimensions and have a supported numeric/boolean data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 5 (the matrix to transpose must have positive dimensions for its last two axes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (all shape dimensions of the input tensor must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 7 (the input tensor must have a numeric or boolean data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 8 (if the input tensor has dimensions, the size of its last dimension must be at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 1
